   194	  agent in one session — the default. A hand-off to a subagent must pay for itself: it has its own objective
   195	  check, or needs a different kind (a blind reviewer, another engine), or its context would not fit. EJ's
   196	  experience (2026-10-02, unmeasured here): a prompt finished by the main agent is faster than the same work split
   197	  over three subagents going back and forth, from the waiting and from context lost at every hand-off. Same
   198	  warning as 3.4: fixed cost per agent, context lost at every split, more joins.
   199	- Output: one row per piece in the state file — steps · deliverable · category · default pattern, engine and check
   200	  from the table · and the node it merges into. The node contract still names the exact model and effort.
